{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrxSsh9d2v4M4tfAksgH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`bash test.sh` now passes (all four suites, exit 0). The fix is in `src/service/resendPolicy.ts`, where `E-THROTTLE` is now in the resend list. Failed alerts with that code go back to the queue and are sent in the next dispatch run. The report shows them as \"발송\" in that run.\n\nI did not add `E-CARRIER`, even though the request asked for both. The agency contract (`docs/sms-agency.md`, §3) says the agency re-queues E-CARRIER itself and retries within 30 minutes, and it bills for that send without notifying us. If we resend it too, customers get duplicate texts and the agency bills twice, which is the INC-0719 problem. If the agency confirms that doesn't happen, adding `\"E-CARRIER\"` to the set is a one-line change.\n\nI also added a 2.2.0 entry to `CHANGELOG.md`. The test files and `test.sh` are unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":45575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9fa39693-bcd1-4fe4-9db0-86f44bca2057","uuid":"c8d69b48-6dae-4e70-9140-97b4341a55e9","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:11:40.290Z","request_id":"req_011CfrxSsSGvRrZtmD9Disvd"}
